From 1966466b241bd55915975bcfafb198539adbc239 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:58:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] perf(runtime): default the frame-rate gate to 60 on the
 Android shell

The gate existed but nothing turned it on. With no stored choice the parser
returns "off", so every draw loop ran at the display's rate - on a 120Hz phone
that is twice the frames and twice the work, which is the largest lever this app
has before any individual renderer is touched.

- platform.isAndroidShell: presence of the shell's `window.foliaAndroid` bridge
  rather than a user agent, so the same build in a phone browser is not mistaken
  for the packaged app.
- frameRateLimiter.ensureVisualizerFrameRateDefault seeds the value into storage
  instead of handing it straight to the limiter, so the graphics setting and the
  gate cannot disagree - that setting reads the same key. The check is for the
  key's presence, not its truthiness: an explicit "off" is still a choice.
- index.tsx seeds it before installing the limiter. Desktop and browser builds
  are untouched and keep unlimited frames.
